LOK: outside Windows an asked update names every DDE source

0086 names a DDE source when its update fails. Outside Windows svl's
DDE is a stub (svl/unx/source/svdde/ddedummy.cxx): every connection
reports no error and carries no data. In Calc a link to a server that
is not there updated as if it were read; in Writer the field's update
succeeded with an empty answer, so its saved text became empty. No DDE
server can answer there, so Calc and Writer leave each DDE link alone
and name it as not read.

diff --git a/sc/source/ui/docshell/docsh4.cxx b/sc/source/ui/docshell/docsh4.cxx
--- a/sc/source/ui/docshell/docsh4.cxx
+++ b/sc/source/ui/docshell/docsh4.cxx
@@ -325,10 +325,15 @@
         }
         else if (auto pDde = dynamic_cast<ScDdeLink*>(xLink.get()))
         {
+#ifdef _WIN32
             if (pDde->Update())
                 bDde = true;
             else
                 rFailed.push_back(pDde->GetAppl() + "|" + pDde->GetTopic());
+#else
+            // DDE is Windows only; elsewhere it never reads.
+            rFailed.push_back(pDde->GetAppl() + "|" + pDde->GetTopic());
+#endif
         }
         else if (auto pWeb = dynamic_cast<ScWebServiceLink*>(xLink.get()))
         {
